-- Every element's text is read like any line of text: inline elements,
-- escapes and $names work in it. Its layout decides how its lines combine.
@let name htmlang

-- Headings, list items, cells, buttons and labels
@h2 Welcome to {@text [color #3b82f6] $name}
@ul
  @li Read {@link /docs the docs}
@table > @tr
  @td Press {@kbd Ctrl}
  @th \{not an element\}
@button [type=button] Save {@text [font-weight bold] now}
@label Name {@abbr [title=required] *}

-- A row or column: each line is a child
@row [spacing 8]
  one
  two

-- A text element: lines flow, whatever writes them
@button [type=button]
  Read
  more
@paragraph
  Items:
  @each $x in a, b
    $x
  @if true
    and done.

-- @code and @textarea show their text as written
@paragraph
  Write {@code {@link /x y}} for a link to {@code $name}.
@code {@b not bold}
@textarea [aria-label=Notes]
  {@b line one}
  line two

-- At the top of the page, two lines of text are two lines
Top
level
